Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 12:14:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Verify a filtered master as air, not music:
 --master-chain mode, and six tests that prove it can fail

A matched master used to be unpublishable: the gate demanded sample-identity with
the approved takes, and any EQ or room tone breaks that by construction. It now
re-applies the declared chain to the dry master and measures what the chain ADDED,
in the pauses only - level against the declared air target, per-second spread,
the level difference between speech and gaps, spectral flatness and peakiness,
and the time lag. A room tone passes; a 220 Hz hum, a side-chained bed, a 10 ms
shift and a 9 dB hot floor all fail, and tests/test_master_chain.py asserts each
of those without rendering anything.

The gallery README gains the price of each voice in words: at 2.507 words/s the
round-three budget is 1585 words over 632.5 s, and only voice-07, voice-13 and
voice-11 are measured at or above that pace - every slower pick means cutting
meaning, since stretching and silence padding are both forbidden here.

MEMORY records the fresh-sandbox recovery in order (the reset to 9048ea7 happened
mid-turn), that the source video and the background bed are both tracked and the
bed rebuilds in three seconds, that a missing faster-whisper wheel is what makes
uncovered speech jump 11.74 s to 29.34 s in a new environment, and that an
archive-rebuilt master legitimately differs by hash from the original run while
reproducing the plan exactly - so --plan and --narration must come from one run.

